The goal is to provide meaningful responses to consumers, maintain clean code, and ensure production issues can be diagnosed quickly."
"In one project, multiple microservices were returning different error formats, which made troubleshooting difficult for frontend and integration teams. I implemented a centralized exception-handling framework using @RestControllerAdvice and standardized error responses across all APIs. This improved API consistency, reduced debugging time, and provided better visibility into production issues."
public class ResourceNotFoundException extends RuntimeException {
    public ResourceNotFoundException(String message) {
        super(message);
    }
}
@RestControllerAdvice
public class GlobalExceptionHandler {
    @ExceptionHandler(ResourceNotFoundException.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleResourceNotFound(
            ResourceNotFoundException ex) {
        ErrorResponse error = new ErrorResponse(
                LocalDateTime.now(),
                HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND.value(),
                ex.getMessage());
        return new ResponseEntity<>(error, HttpStatus.NOT_FOUND);
    }
    @ExceptionHandler(Exception.class)
    public ResponseEntity<ErrorResponse> handleGenericException(
            Exception ex) {
        ErrorResponse error = new ErrorResponse(
                LocalDateTime.now(),
                HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR.value(),
                "Something went wrong");
        return new ResponseEntity<>(error,
                HttpStatus.INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
    }
}

